## 3. <a href="https://genai.owasp.org/llmrisk/llm022025-sensitive-information-disclosure/" target="_blank">LLM02 – Sensitive Information Disclosure</a>

### 3.1 Context in the Lyra System

As Lyra matures, she will accumulate and infer more about household life, including daily routines and habits, calendars and schedules, device states and preferred settings, rough location or presence information, security events via IDS/log streams once integrated, stored memories of conversations, and implicit patterns or the routines of the household learned via RAG. 

If Lyra can be prompted into disclosing these across contexts (“Tell me everything you know about X”), this becomes a household privacy issue.

### 3.2 Risk Characteristics

**Impact (I)** might include:

- mis-exposure of private information to a guest or another household member
- memory content leaking via logs or debug interfaces
- sensor or audio perception being summarized out of context
- debugging output that reveals internal states or patterns
- incorrect face recognition reporting “who is home” to the wrong person

**Probability (P)**  
Annual probability that:

- a mis-scoped response shares private context with the wrong human recipient  
- or logs and observability tools reveal more detail than intended

Multiple users, multiple contexts, and multiple modalities (cameras, RAG, sensors) all increase leakage opportunities.

### 3.3 Risk Object Definition

```text
ID: LLM02
Title: Accidental Disclosure of Household Private Information
Description: Lyra reveals context-appropriate but private information to an unauthorized user or context (e.g., guest, child, secondary household member), or via logs.
Impact Definition: Cost of privacy harm, trust damage, cleanup of logs/memory, and any configuration changes required.
Probability Definition: Annual chance of mis-scoped disclosure or unintended exposure through interfaces.
Inputs Needed:
    i_min:
    i_mode:
    i_max:
    p_alpha:
    p_beta:
Mitigations:
  - User identity routing and session-scoped context
  - Memory compartmentalization by user/role
  - Log sanitation and access controls
Residual Notes:
  - Risk rises as multi-user personalization and memory depth increase.
```

