## 7. <a href="https://genai.owasp.org/llmrisk/llm062025-excessive-agency/" target="_blank">LLM06 – Excessive Agency</a>

### 7.1 Context in the Lyra System

With expanded authority, Lyra may:

- control IoT devices and Home Assistant
- write or edit configuration files
- schedule events or reminders
- query and act on location and traffic data
- manage routines (e.g., lights, fans, environmental systems)
- interact with OS-level tools or scripts (if enabled)
- issue outbound HTTP calls to local services

The risk is not autonomous intent, but **over-privileged tools and insufficient guardrails**, causing:

- tool misuse
- malformed outputs feeding tools
- cascading failures in automations
- overconfidence in performing multi-step tasks

### 7.2 Risk Characteristics

**Impact (I)** can include:

- incorrect or inconvenient home automations
- missed or incorrect reminders
- time lost debugging and restoring configurations
- possible physical impact (comfort, lighting, HVAC behavior)
- higher if connected to any safety-relevant systems

**Probability (P)**  
Annual probability that:

- a misrouted tool call or malformed command  
- causes a non-trivial problem in the home environment

This risk rises as more tools are added and as Lyra is trusted with more complex task chains.

### 7.3 Risk Object Definition

```text
ID: LLM06
Title: Harmful Outcomes from Over-Privileged Tools
Description: Lyra misuses tools or chains tools in unintended ways (e.g., misconfiguring home automation, editing critical files, or issuing dangerous commands).
Impact Definition: Cost of restoring automation, configurations, and any physical-world effects.
Probability Definition: Annual chance that tool misuse leads to noticeable negative impact.
Inputs Needed:
    i_min:
    i_mode:
    i_max:
    p_alpha:
    p_beta:
Mitigations:
  - Human-in-the-loop confirmation for sensitive actions
  - Scoping tools to narrow, reversible actions
  - Isolation of higher-risk tools in separate microservices
Residual Notes:
  - Strongly tied to the design of Lyra’s action and authority layer.
```

