## 9. <a href="https://genai.owasp.org/llmrisk/llm082025-vector-and-embedding-weaknesses/" target="_blank">LLM08 – Vector DB / Embedding Weaknesses</a>

### 9.1 Context in the Lyra System

Embeddings become the primary knowledge substrate. Risks include:

- embedding inversion (reconstruction of sensitive content from vectors)
- adversarial or specially crafted embeddings
- “benign-looking” text that warps RAG retrieval
- semantic collisions and ambiguous embeddings
- stale or contradictory documents degrading retrieval quality
- contamination across years of incremental ingest

### 9.2 Risk Characteristics

**Impact (I)** may be:

- systematic retrieval of wrong or misleading documents
- subtle but persistent reasoning errors
- debugging and reindexing efforts
- potential privacy concerns if embeddings are misused or exfiltrated

**Probability (P)**  
Annual probability that:

- vector space weaknesses cause materially incorrect retrieval  
- or allow reconstruction/leakage of sensitive text from embeddings

Probability increases sharply with automated ingestion, larger corpora, more embedding models, or untrusted sources.

### 9.3 Risk Object Definition

```text
ID: LLM08
Title: Vector Store Attacks or Semantic Collisions
Description: Adversarial or malformed embeddings distort retrieval or leak semantic information, causing systematic reasoning errors or privacy issues.
Impact Definition: Cost of debugging RAG behavior, cleaning the vector store, and adjusting embedding models or ingestion rules.
Probability Definition: Annual chance that vector-space issues cause harmful or misleading retrieval.
Inputs Needed:
    i_min:
    i_mode:
    i_max:
    p_alpha:
    p_beta:
Mitigations:
  - Strict control of ingestion sources
  - Regular audits of high-impact content
  - Optionally, embedding model rotation or ensemble strategies
Residual Notes:
  - Closely related to LLM04; can be treated jointly or separately in the risk register.
```

