## <a href="https://genai.owasp.org/llmrisk/llm092025-misinformation/" target="_blank">10. LLM09 – Misinformation / Reliance</a>

### 10.1 Context in the Lyra System

Lyra will act as a decision support engine for the household and will be asked questions such as:

- “What’s the best route to X?”
- “When should we leave for the airport?”
- “Is this medication interaction safe?” (even if discouraged)
- “What are the tides at time/place?”
- “Why is home automation rule Y failing?”
- “Which contractor option seems most appropriate?”

Incorrect answers can have tangible real-world cost in time, money, or safety.

### 10.2 Risk Characteristics

**Impact (I)** ranges from:

- minor annoyances and small rework
- moderate travel or scheduling disruptions
- poor choices in services, purchases, or configuration

**Probability (P)**  
Even with RAG and external APIs, hallucination and data error are persistent.  
Annual probability covers:

- consequential misinterpretation of tools or APIs
- hallucinations that appear trustworthy
- user acting on information without cross-checking

This is a low-impact, high-frequency category that can accumulate significant ALE over time.

### 10.3 Risk Object Definition

```text
